WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.280
In the story of Exodus,
after the golden calf,

2
00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.400
Moses brings two new tablets of stone.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.270
There, the text says,
God proclaims his name:

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.030
merciful and gracious, slow to anger.

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.790
Those words travel.

6
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.200
Moses prays them.

7
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.970
Psalms sing them.

8
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.560
A prophet calls people back with them.

9
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:26.870
Then a prophet called Jonah throws
the same words back at God, angry.

10
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.790
Why would anyone quote
words of mercy in anger?

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.900
In this mission, you'll read the sentence
closely and trace it across the Old

12
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.110
Testament.

13
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.810
Then you'll hear God argue
with himself in Hosea,

14
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.810
and meet laws that protect the vulnerable.

15
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:47.490
Your mission: find out why a prophet
quoted God's own words of mercy in anger.
